# Copy to .env.local for local development. Nothing here is a secret.

# Gives the learning section one public address: https://learn.sushantgundla.com
#
# Set to exactly `1` to turn it on. Unset, or any other value, means today's
# behaviour: the section is served at sushantgundla.com/learn and nothing
# redirects.
#
# With it on:
#   - sushantgundla.com/learn/... redirects (308) to learn.sushantgundla.com/...
#   - every /learn page declares its canonical URL on the subdomain
#   - the /learn URLs are dropped from sushantgundla.com's sitemap
#   - localhost is untouched, so `npm run dev` still serves /learn
#
# Where it goes: the Vercel project's Environment Variables, Production scope.
#
# ORDER MATTERS. Only turn this on after BOTH of these are true, or every
# visitor to the section is sent to a host that does not resolve:
#   1. learn.sushantgundla.com has been added under the Vercel project's Domains
#   2. its DNS CNAME points at Vercel and resolves
#
# It is a NEXT_PUBLIC_ variable so client components read the same switch, which
# means the value is baked in at build time — after changing it, redeploy in
# Vercel for it to take effect.
NEXT_PUBLIC_LEARN_SUBDOMAIN_LIVE=
